<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bob Marley</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1945">1945</a>–<a href="/years/1981">1981</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Robert Nesta Marley</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bob Marley was a Jamaican singer and songwriter who brought reggae to a worldwide audience with his band the Wailers. A follower of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rastafari">Rastafari</a>, he wrote songs of spiritual faith, protest and love, such as No Woman, No Cry, Get Up, Stand Up and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/redemption-song">Redemption Song</a>. He remains <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a>'s best-known cultural figure; he died of cancer in 1981 aged 36.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bob-marley.jpg" alt="Bob Marley" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Not credited · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bob_Marley_circa_1976_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…African historical scholarship, among them Diop and the Nigerian historian Kenneth Onwuka Dike, and its cultural side flourished in the Négritude poets, the First World Festival of Negro Arts in Dakar in 1966, the festival known as FESTAC in Lagos in 1977 and the reggae of <b>Bob Marley</b>.</blockquote><a href="/movement/pan-africanism">Pan-Africanism · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>&quot;Redemption Song&quot; is the last track of Uprising, the twelfth album of <b>Bob Marley</b> and the Wailers, produced by Chris Blackwell and released by Island Records in 1980.</blockquote><a href="/songs/redemption-song">Redemption Song</a></li><li><blockquote>Rastafari and reggae, led by <b>Bob Marley</b>, made Jamaican culture globally influential.</blockquote><a href="/state/jamaica">Jamaica</a></li></ul></section>
